# Packages from omarchy-base.packages not attempted by default on aarch64,
# because building them here is expensive and buys nothing. Two reasons qualify:
# there is no aarch64 build and the attempt compiles a dependency chain for
# hours before failing anyway, or the package builds fine but something already
# installed satisfies what depends on it, so the result is discarded. Most
# unavailable packages fail their architecture check in seconds and cost
# nothing; only the expensive ones are listed. Measured on a clean Apple
# Silicon install.
#
# This is a default, not a verdict. The installer offers to build them anyway
# when it has a terminal, and OMARCHY_TRY_UNAVAILABLE=1 forces the attempt, so
# an entry that gains ARM support later costs a prompt rather than being wrong
# forever. Drop it from this list once it builds.

# obs-studio resolves to obs-studio-browser, whose chain builds ffmpeg-obs
# (134 min), svt-av1-hdr10plus-git (26 min), vlc-luajit (18 min) and
# libajantv2 before svt-av1-hdr10plus-git and libhdr10plus-rs-git fail their
# aarch64 architecture check. Roughly 183 minutes for nothing.
obs-studio

# dotnet-runtime ships in Arch's x86_64 extra repo, but Arch Linux ARM has no
# package under that name and neither does the AUR (only the -bin variants), so
# yay fails it immediately. Listed so the install skips it cleanly rather than
# emitting a misleading "skipped" warning for a package that cannot install here.
dotnet-runtime

# quickshell-git builds on aarch64 -- and then the build is thrown away. The
# omarchy package depends on plain `quickshell`, which Arch Linux ARM now ships
# in extra (0.3.0-2), so pacman satisfies the dependency from the repo and the
# freshly compiled quickshell-git is never installed. Measured on a clean
# install: the artifact sat unused in yay's cache while `pacman -Qi quickshell`
# reported the repo package installed as a dependency of omarchy. Skipping it
# changes nothing about what ends up on the machine, and drops a Qt/C++ compile
# plus its cli11 and vulkan-headers makedepends from every install.
quickshell-git
